cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the abstract below and the MorphoNAS engine paper listed under references."
type: software
title: "MorphoNAS-DevPriors: reproducibility companion for 'Grown, not trained: what a developmental map makes likely before selection'"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-09-12
abstract: >-
  Code, data, and analysis scripts behind the study of the functional prior that
  un-evolved MorphoNAS development places on a recurrent network before any learning
  or selection. The headline is a size/density-controlled Mantel-Haenszel comparison
  against matched-random wiring, with a paired reward-axis de-confounder showing the
  enrichment is outcome-dependent. The repository also includes exploratory full-paper
  material: a cross-family map, an observation-axis de-confounder, a feedback-arc-set
  recurrence ablation and a structural recurrence measure, a competence-threshold
  robustness sweep, and structured indirect-encoding (CPPN/HyperNEAT) baselines, whose
  mechanisms are not yet isolated.
